  {
   "type": "hotspots",
   "header": "<h1> »smartCheck 600/800« - top model for the highest demands </h1>",
   "intro": "",
   "img": {
    "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/5/9/csm_smartcheck600_infodots_18eab80454.webp",
    "alt": "",
    "w": 1340,
    "h": 990
   },
   "spots": [
    {
     "x": 38.181,
     "y": 21.366,
     "label": "One-hand operating handle »eQ«",
     "text": "<h3>One-hand operating handle »eQ«</h3> <h4>Ergonomic one-hand operating handle »eQ«</h4> <p>Ergonomic one-hand operating handle »eQ« (ergonomic &amp; quick) - to easily move the optics carrier to the correct position in the Z and X axes. The button with the Solutions symbol can be individually configured with additional practical functions, making operation even easier and more convenient.</p>"
    },
    {
     "x": 22.424,
     "y": 43.338,
     "label": "X-axis",
     "text": "<h3>X-axis</h3> <h4>X-axis</h4> <p><strong>X-axis manual/CNC - </strong>the high-precision and smooth-running linear axes are used for quick and fine positioning of the measuring optics to the tool cutting edge. Whether manually for spot checks using the »eQ« single-handed operating handle or CNC-controlled for fully automatic processes, they enable reliable, fast and convenient measurement.</p> <p><strong>Manual fine adjustment - </strong>the alternative to CNC control. The ergonomic handwheels for additional manual fine adjustment of the Z and X axes are particularly suitable for the tool inspection module.</p>"
    },
    {
     "x": 34.881,
     "y": 44.87,
     "label": "Y-axis",
     "text": "<h3>Y-axis</h3> <h4>Y-axis</h4> <p>Y-axis - the optional, CNC-controlled linear axis for measuring off-center cutting edges on turning or multifunctional tools.</p>"
    },
    {
     "x": 6.043,
     "y": 58.982,
     "label": "Storage shelf",
     "text": "<h3>Storage shelf</h3> <h4>Practical storage shelf</h4> <p>Practical storage shelf - holds attachment holders, adapters, tools and intermediate sockets.</p>"
    },
    {
     "x": 48.131,
     "y": 22.052,
     "label": "Incident light camera",
     "text": "<h3>Incident light camera</h3> <h4>Tool inspection with manually swiveling incident light camera</h4> <p>Tool inspection with manually swiveling incident light camera - for radial and axial inspection and measuring tasks. Integrated multi-LED ring light segmented into eight areas ensures optimum illumination of the surface with adjustable light intensity. The clamping and locking device as well as the swivel range of -30° to 90° ensure an ideal perspective for the respective measuring point.</p>"
    },
    {
     "x": 78.85,
     "y": 18.762,
     "label": "Software »pilot 4.0«",
     "text": "<h3>Software »pilot 4.0«</h3> <h4>»pilot 4.0« software</h4> <p>»pilot 4.0« software - is self-explanatory, clear and enables the operator to take reliable measurements. It offers a uniform user interface on all ZOLLER systems - right up to ZOLLER TMS Tool Management Solutions. The individual structure of the software allows customer-specific adaptations to be implemented quickly.</p> <p>Integrated operating unit - offers health-friendly and comfortable working. The 24\" TFT color monitor can be individually adapted to the needs of each operator: The height, swivel and tilt angle can be flexibly adjusted.</p>"
    },
    {
     "x": 48.342,
     "y": 43.812,
     "label": "High-precision spindle",
     "text": "<h3>High-precision spindle</h3> <h4>High-precision spindle »ace«</h4> <p>High-precision spindle »ace« - guarantees μm-precise holding and clamping of tools and holders of all kinds. Adaptation to many tool holder systems is guaranteed by the universal attachment holder changing system. The optional CNC drive with autofocus and precise angle measuring system offers automatic focusing of the tool cutting edge and recording of the cutting contour.</p>"
    },
    {
     "x": 74.745,
     "y": 47.933,
     "label": "Separate control unit",
     "text": "<h3>Separate control unit</h3> <h4>Separate »cockpit« control unit</h4> <p>Separate »cockpit« operating unit - offers space for keyboard and mouse as well as shelves for label and laser printers, scanners and tools. The height and angle of the 24\" TFT color monitor can be adjusted to make using the software as comfortable as possible. This means that every operator can set up the workstation individually in just a few simple steps.</p>"
    },
    {
     "x": 48.931,
     "y": 81.138,
     "label": "Under table",
     "text": "<h3>Under table</h3> <h4>Stable underbench</h4> <p>Stable underbench - the basis of the appliance: This is where the computer, electronics and pneumatic elements are housed in an industrial and service-friendly manner, all neatly laid out with sufficient space for good accessibility and optimum ventilation.</p>"
    },
    {
     "x": 34.383,
     "y": 31.508,
     "label": "Z-axis",
     "text": "<h3>Z-axis</h3> <h4>Z-axis</h4> <p><strong>Z-axis manual/CNC - </strong>the high-precision and smooth-running linear axes are used for quick and fine positioning of the measuring optics to the tool cutting edge. Whether manually for spot checks using the »eQ« single-handed operating handle or CNC-controlled for fully automatic processes, they enable reliable, fast and convenient measurement.</p> <p><strong>Manual fine adjustment - </strong>the alternative to CNC control. The ergonomic handwheels for additional manual fine adjustment of the Z and X axes are particularly suitable for the tool inspection module.</p>"
    }
   ],
